<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36332" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pimplēus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Piplēus</span></b> ), a, um,
		adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Pimplean</i> (v. Pimpleis); hence, <i>sacred to
				the Muses</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					105, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 11, 3</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pimplēa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pi-plēa</span></b> ),
			ae, f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A Muse</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">necte meo Lamiae coronam, Pimplea dulcis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 26, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>The fountain of Pimpla</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1,
				4, 25</span></i>.</div>
